      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the whole \"game\" feels rigged, the question of why to keep playing becomes profoundly heavy. It is completely understandable to feel cynical and hopeless when facing such systemic failure. However, sometimes the victory isn't in winning the flawed system, but in creating a small, self-contained space of integrity outside of it. You might need to shift focus from \"winning\" life to simply safeguarding your own peace amidst the disorder.",
      "source": "target",
